  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "**Method 1** \n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $5$ units, so the distance equals $5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14146131/assets/8e367b3fe7f6c0f6d7e2fa68569b359bfaac855e588a3a2e3f6e2afb133edde4.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14146131/assets/2cb5654bcbd1d8cf5fc7f612d92d264ae4945c542db4d4a8c90a7e8829adf2d9.png)\n\nThe point $(6,4)$ is at a distance of $6$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $(1,4)$ is at a distance of $1$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $6-1=5.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
